<TbStack Row Gap="2" Wrap>
    <TbButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="() => _noHeader = true">Without a header</TbButton>
    <TbButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="() => _noClose = true">Without a close button</TbButton>
    <TbButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="() => _rich = true">With an icon in the title</TbButton>
    <TbButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="() => _actions = true">With header actions</TbButton>
    <TbButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="() => _own = true">With its own header</TbButton>
</TbStack>

<TbDialog @bind-Open="_noHeader" Title="Trail closed" Options="new() { ShowHeader = false }">
    <TbText>The title still names this dialog for screen readers.</TbText>
    <TbDialogActions><TbButton OnClick="() => _noHeader = false">Done</TbButton></TbDialogActions>
</TbDialog>
<TbDialog @bind-Open="_noClose" Title="Trail reopened" Options="new() { CloseButton = false }">
    <TbText>Press the button below, or Escape, to close this dialog.</TbText>
    <TbDialogActions><TbButton OnClick="() => _noClose = false">Done</TbButton></TbDialogActions>
</TbDialog>
<TbDialog @bind-Open="_rich" Title="Trail folder">
    <TbDialogTitle><TbIcon Icon="ExampleIcons.Folder" /> Trail folder</TbDialogTitle>
    <TbText>The icon sits beside the title and is hidden from screen readers.</TbText>
    <TbDialogActions><TbButton OnClick="() => _rich = false">Done</TbButton></TbDialogActions>
</TbDialog>
<TbDialog @bind-Open="_actions" Title="Trail notes" Options="new() { Modal = false, Draggable = true }">
    <TbDialogHeaderActions>
        <TbMenu AriaLabel="Note options" Icon="ExampleIcons.ChevronDown" Size="Size.Small" Align="PlacementAlign.End">
            <TbMenuItem>Pin the notes</TbMenuItem>
            <TbMenuItem>Copy a link</TbMenuItem>
        </TbMenu>
    </TbDialogHeaderActions>
    <TbText>The menu sits in the header but stays out of the dialog's name, and dragging the header moves the
        dialog.</TbText>
    <TbDialogActions><TbButton OnClick="() => _actions = false">Done</TbButton></TbDialogActions>
</TbDialog>
<TbDialog @bind-Open="_own" Title="Camp checklist" Options="new() { Modal = false, Draggable = true }">
    <TbDialogHeader>
        <TbStack Row Gap="2" Align="Align.Center" Justify="Justify.SpaceBetween">
            <TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle" As="TextElement.Span">Camp checklist</TbText>
            <TbButton Size="Size.Small" Variant="Variant.Text" OnClick="() => _own = false">Close</TbButton>
        </TbStack>
    </TbDialogHeader>
    <TbText>This header is the page's own, with its own Close button. Dragging it moves the dialog.</TbText>
</TbDialog>

@code {
    private bool _noHeader;
    private bool _noClose;
    private bool _rich;
    private bool _actions;
    private bool _own;
}
